From 6ce3871e277ebe03b6a32d7bac841207ec0bd9d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SixVolts <rigel@sixvolts.org>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/03] rdna-boosts: rdna2 block 02: fa tile Q from global half2 for the wide kernels

Port of sixvolts/llama-halo-hybrid 40408c28 + 4d93e972: the wide tile kernels
(ncols >= 16, DKQ <= 256) read Q from a pre-converted global half2 buffer
(flash_attn_q_to_half2, launched by launch_fattn when q_h2) instead of staging Q
in shared memory; on RDNA2 the K reads already saturate the LDS, and removing
the Q LDS traffic measured +30% on the 512-column kernel. Gated at compile time
by GGML_CUDA_FATTN_TILE_Q_GLOBAL (HIP + RDNA2) and at runtime by the host-side
rdna2 test; the narrow kernels and every other device keep the original Q_tmp
path. Q_tmp shrinks to a 2-element stub when q_global (RDNA2 has 64 KB LDS per
WGP).
---

 0 files changed

